# Overload — environment variables.
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) for local development. NEVER commit real secrets.
#
# Environment model:
#   • LOCAL dev  → the Supabase CLI stack (`npx supabase start`, Docker). No cloud project.
#   • PRODUCTION → a single Supabase cloud project named `overload-prod`.
# There is no dev cloud project and no staging tier. Vercel deploys production
# only (no DB-backed preview deployments); verify changes locally and in prod.
#
# WARNING: anything that reads `.env` (prisma CLI, `next dev`/`next build`, the
# exercise import) uses whatever is here. Keep LOCAL values in `.env`; put
# production values in Vercel, and pass them on the command line only for the
# deliberate, runbook-driven production steps.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT — values for the `npx supabase start` stack.
# `supabase start` prints the Project URL, the DB URL, and two keys:
#   • "Publishable" (sb_publishable_…) → NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#   • "Secret"      (sb_secret_…)      → SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY (import only)
# Re-print them any time with `npx supabase status -o env` (PUBLISHABLE_KEY and
# SECRET_KEY). Older CLIs call these the "anon" and "service_role" keys
# (ANON_KEY / SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, long eyJ… JWTs); either form works.
# The defaults below match a standard local stack (ports from
# supabase/config.toml).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Server-only (NEVER prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_). Local stack Postgres (port 54322).
# Local has no separate pooler, so DATABASE_URL and DIRECT_URL are the same.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres

# Public (safe to ship). Local API gateway + the local "Publishable" key printed
# by `npx supabase start` (a shared local default, not a secret).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<"Publishable" key (sb_publishable_…) from `npx supabase start`>

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXERCISE CATALOG IMPORT ONLY (`npm run db:seed`) — Library & Gyms Setup.
# The service-role ("Secret") key is used ONLY by the import process to write
# exercise images to Storage. It is NEVER read by the app, NEVER set in Vercel,
# and NEVER prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_. Locally, set it in `.env`; `npm run db:seed`
# fails with "SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is not set." without it.
# For production, never put it in a file: pass it on the command line for the
# one runbook-driven import only.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<"Secret" key (sb_secret_…) from `npx supabase start`>
#
# The import refuses a non-local DATABASE_URL unless this equals its host
# (protects production from an accidental run). Set it only on the command line
# for the one deliberate production import — see the Library & Gyms runbook.
# OVERLOAD_IMPORT_CONFIRM_HOST=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TESTS — throwaway LOCAL Postgres for integration tests, reset between tests.
# MUST NOT point at any Supabase database (local stack or prod). If unset, the
# integration harness provisions an embedded throwaway Postgres automatically.
# Tests NEVER fall back to DATABASE_URL.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://overload_test:overload_test@127.0.0.1:5433/overload_test
